Out of memory error due to meta space:

In meta space the class definitions are stored, when we load multiple class files at run time or multiple jars at a time, at a point of time the metaspace
becomes saturated then the out of memory error occurs.

Simulation:
-----------
public class solution{
public static void main(String[] args){
ClassPool classpool=ClassPool.getDefault();
int counter=0;
while(true){
String name="Buggy Class";
classpool.makeClass(name).toClass();
count++;
if(count%5000==0){
System.out.println(count+ "Classes Created");
}
}
}
}

