Reason 5:Permgen:
---------
Its replace by metaspace out of the heap. 
1. Before the java 8, the permgen was present in the heap, we used to store the class definition in the permgen. 
2. PermGen space is prone to causing the famous OutOfMemoryError due to its fixed size and inefficient garbage collection. 
This error often occurs when class loaders are not properly garbage collected, leading to memory leaks. This is particularly 
common in development environments where new class loaders are frequently created.
3. Starting with Java 8, PermGen was replaced by Metaspace, which brought significant improvements. Unlike PermGen, Metaspace uses native memory and can grow automatically by default, reducing the likelihood of OutOfMemoryError. Metaspace also introduces new flags for tuning memory, such as MetaspaceSize and MaxMetaspaceSize.

