Reason 6: Unable to create new native threads:
--------------------------------------
1. When your application has no memory to create to the threads anymore, then this error is thrown

a. For Analyzing the thread dump Fast Thread tool.
b. It will give you the complete summary like what and all the threads that are runable or in timed waiting state. 
c. Groups the threads with identical stack trace and groups them under 1 category.

Causes:
1. Threads are leaking, fpr every call a new thread is being created.
2. When your thread count goes behind the kernel default thread limit.

Troubleshooting:
-----------------
1. Make use of thread dump. Identify the thread leaks (Creating a new thread for every call and not terminating).
2. Make use of the tools like Fast Heap, then analyse it using this tools like Fast Thread. Example if your threads are using same

Fixes:
-----
1.Fix the code where it causing the thread leaks. 
2. Increase the thread limit of the OS kernel.


Reason 7: Direct Buffer Memory:
------------------------------
1. When we do the direct file io operation those files will be stored here in the Buffer io area.
2. When you have high i/0 performing requirement and huge buffers are allocated to that task but never released then those it may get saturated and throw this error.
3. In Stack trace itself it prints the message.

Causes:
-----
1. Increase in the direct buffer usage
  a. Moving from spring framework rest template to the webclient/
  b. java.nio package
  c. Some JDBC Drivers.

Fixes:
------
1. Fix your memory leakes
2. Increase the MaxDirectMemorySize

