Reason 8: Kill process or sacrifice child:
---------------------------------------
It occurs when there is not that much RAM capacity, then the Kernel will think that the JVM is requesting much memory, it will terminate your JVM.
-> It will be stored in the kernel logs:.
Causes:
1. LAck of RAM capacity.
2. High Memory utilisation by other process in the environment.
3. Memory leak in the code.

Solution:
---------
1. Kill other processes.
2. Increase RAM capacity.
3. Fix Memory leak in the code.

